  "query_preview": "..High pressure remains across the state today with \nsimilar conditions expected through this evening. Expect showers and \nthunderstorms to form across the higher terrain this afternoon, then \ngradually pushing towards the west into this evening. With some \ninstability present we could see some stronger to possibly severe \nstorms. Heavy rain with the potential for localized flooding will \nalso be possible as storm motions remain on the slower side and we\ncould see some training of storms. \n\nHeat will also continue in the lower elevations of the Grand Canyon\nand Glen and Marble Canyons. The Extreme Heat Warning was extended\nfor these areas through 8 PM Saturday. It looks like the heat will\nbreak once the high becomes settled over the Four Corners and we \nsee moisture finally push into northern Arizona, bringing increased\nchances for showers and thunderstorms.\n\nThe active pattern looks to hold through next week as the high looks \nto remain near or over the Four Corners. Temperatures will cool but \nwill still remain above normal through the period. Overall, expect \nthe monsoon to be the main story for at least the next week.",
